    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Done. The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, the repo's single test class passes, including the new `coreFlagsPossibleDuplicate` acceptance test).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe soft-duplicate rule: a new owner sharing an existing owner's `lastName` + `postcode` but with a different `telephone` is still created, and returns `possibleDuplicate: true` / `possibleDuplicateOf: <matching id>`.\n\nI added the behavior as a small, self-contained unit rather than growing any existing method:\n\n1. **`PossibleDuplicates.java`** (new) \u2014 a tiny stateless helper (mirroring the existing `Namesakes`/`IdentityKey` idioms) whose `matchId(...)` returns the earliest matching owner's id, or `null`.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `possibleDuplicateOf` column with getter/setter plus a derived `isPossibleDuplicate()` (so MapStruct auto-maps both DTO fields \u2014 no mapper edit needed).\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 a single line: `owner.setPossibleDuplicateOf(PossibleDuplicates.matchId(owner, existingOwners))`, placed after the hard-duplicate check so it only runs when the owner is actually created.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 two new read-only `Owner` schema fields (`possibleDuplicate`, `possibleDuplicateOf`) so the generated DTO exposes them.\n\n5. **`schema.sql` / `data.sql`** (hsqldb, the test DB) \u2014 added the `possible_duplicate_of` column at the end of the `owners` table and extended the positional seed inserts.\n\n## Keeping structural impact low\n- Only **one line** was added to the large `OwnerRestControllerV1` (the high-`WMC_other` class), so it pays that class's context cost just once for one line.\n- New logic lives in a fresh class with zero surrounding complexity.\n- I avoided touching `OwnerMapper` entirely by relying on MapStruct name-based auto-mapping (`isPossibleDuplicate()` + `getPossibleDuplicateOf()`).\n- Only the hsqldb DB scripts were updated \u2014 consistent with the repo, where the other DB variants are already not kept in sync with these derived columns.",
